														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1840839">
									

<p>Actually, that's not accurate. The human ear is only capable of hearing a finite <em>range</em>, but there's an infinite <em>number</em> of tones/frequencies within that range, even if we'd have difficulty discriminating between extremely close ones. And even with a finite number of &quot;discernable&quot; tones, the number of combinations is infinite, because there's no limit on how <em>long</em> the composition is. Add in things like chords, harmonies, variable relative volumes, sustained tone lengths, and effects like deliberate static or fuzzing overlays, and the number of potential sound combinations is literally larger than the number of subatomic particles in the universe.</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>Giving bearhugs to the unsuspecting since 1872.</p>

